<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tristán de Luna y Arellano</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1510">1510</a>–<a href="/years/1573">1573</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Tristán de Luna</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tristán de Luna y Arellano was a Spanish conquistador who in 1559 led a large expedition from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-new-spain">New Spain</a> to found a colony on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pensacola">Pensacola</a> Bay in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>. A hurricane soon destroyed most of his ships and supplies, and detachments sent inland in search of food reached the declining chiefdom of Coosa in 1560. The settlement was abandoned in 1561, after Luna had been replaced as governor.</p></div>
